@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# spmid (OnePlus 6 downstream driver)
+
+`spmid` reads SDM845 SPMI arbiter v5 and PM8998 PON/GPIO buttons, then publishes `K_POWER`, `K_VOLUME_DOWN`, and `K_VOLUME_UP` OrbClient key edges to `inputd`'s producer endpoint. It never writes PMIC registers. Its only MMIO writes are the arbiter observer's CONFIG and CMD0 registers for read transactions. Poll interval is 50 ms (20 wakeups/s); no background start unit is installed.
+
+The current profile uses the static `sdm845.dtsi` window addresses and EE 0. Do not start it on a phone until the live DT and PMIC status polarity have been checked against `specs/spmi-pmic-buttons.md` and the phone oracle. The daemon exits on probe, transaction, or inputd errors. A true Redox aarch64 build and device test remain pending because this host does not have `aarch64-unknown-redox` installed.
+
+Host verification: `cargo test -p spmid-core -p spmid --offline` and `cargo check -p spmid --features host-compile --offline`. The `host-compile` feature compiles the Redox code path with the host standard library; it is a compile check only, not a supported Linux runtime.
